{%- comment -%}
  Zo Veilig — cart guard. Keeps the live cart in the one shape a package purchase may
  have (CLAUDE.md, Pricing pipeline):

      the real package product at quantity pkg_qty (the 3 prepaid months; Shopify's
      automatic "Eerste 3 maanden" discount takes 50% off that line by itself)
    + exactly one installation line at quantity 1 (never discounted)

  A package line is a line whose product_type is `sub_type` and whose handle is one of the
  5 purchasable package handles from pricing.config.json. The Cart AJAX API doesn't expose
  product metafields (custom.finder_key) the way server-side Liquid does, but it does expose
  the handle, and the handle also says which installation model the package uses: Inzicht,
  Zeker and Alert are NAMI, Beschermd and Protect are Climax.

  Runs on load of /cart and /cart?view=overzicht and applies at most ONE fix per load, then
  reloads, so each fix is re-checked against the real cart:

  1. More than one of the 3 NAMI install variants at once (e.g. a stale line left behind
     by an interrupted swap): keep the most recently added, remove the rest.
  2. Quantities. A package line at any quantity other than pkg_qty is set to pkg_qty; a
     second line for the same package (e.g. added from two pages with different line
     properties) is removed, since two lines would be 6 prepaid months; an installation
     line at any quantity other than 1 is set to 1.
  3. A Climax package without the Climax installation line (CL003) gets it added — one
     fixed fee, one correct answer, safe to add on the customer's behalf.
  4. The Climax installation line in a cart with no Climax package is removed: CL003 must
     never be charged for a NAMI package.
  5. The Woning lines (2026-09-25; one per platform since 2026-10-27; Koop packages counted in
     since 2026-10-28): one for the NAMI packages, one for the Climax packages (zv_woning_handles
     / zv_woning_skus, resolved by the caller with zv-woning-variants into woning_variant_ids,
     parallel to woning_applies_by_product). Per Woning product, its target quantity is pkg_qty x
     the floors over ITS OWN package lines' `Woning` properties: a Huren line by its handle
     (woning_applies_by_product), a Koop line by its finder_key (woning_applies_fks_by_product,
     via koop_map) since a Koop line's handle is a different product — zv-woning-floors' values
     and legacy prefix apply either way, so a legacy "Groter dan 100 m²…" value counts as 1
     floor. Never another platform's. More than one line of a product is merged into one at the
     target; a single line at another quantity is set to the target; target 0 removes it; a cart
     with Woning but no line (e.g. a NAMI cart from before 2026-09-25, or any Koop cart before
     2026-10-28) gets the line added.
  6. A package line whose package doesn't offer Woning (not in woning_applies) but carries a
     `Woning` property has it deleted via /cart/change.js, same quantity. Until 2026-10-27 that
     was every Climax line (Beschermd and Protect had no Woning from 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-27);
     today all five packages offer it, so the rule only acts if the config ever takes one out.
     A legacy Abonnement/Uitbreidingen property on it is left alone.
  7. Riders (2026-10-27, rider_pairs 'leadVariant:riderVariant[:cents]|…', from zv-addon-riders):
     the camera subscription rides with ADC-750, the bought Videodeurbel. A cart with a
     lead line keeps exactly one rider line at quantity pkg_qty (added, set or merged); a cart
     without one has its rider lines removed (the customer removed the doorbell on /cart).
     2026-10-28: pkg_qty, not flat 1 — the camera subscription prepays the months like Ontzorgpakket, and like it
     is in the "Eerste 3 maanden" discount (since 2026-10-28), so those months are 50% off: see its addonNames note in pricing.config.json.
  The Woning and rider lines never match the package or installation rules above (their
  product types are not sub_type and their variants are none of the installation ids). A
  Woning product that doesn't resolve (0 in woning_variant_ids) is skipped by rule 5: the
  property-only fallback for its packages.

  Koop package lines (Huren/Kopen, 2026-10-24, docs/koop-checkout-2026-10-24.md): a line with
  the property Afname: Kopen whose handle is one of koop_map's Koop products. It is a one-time
  purchase, never a package line above: rule 2 keeps it at quantity 1 (never pkg_qty) and
  removes a second line for the same Koop product; a bought Climax package counts for rules 3
  and 4 exactly like a rented one (CL003 added, kept). A bought package's Woning choice now
  follows the same path as its Ontzorgpakket add-on (2026-10-28, was property-only since
  2026-10-24 for NAMI / 2026-10-27 for Climax — Odoo had nothing to bill it from): it counts
  towards its platform's Woning line in rule 5 too, matched by finder_key since a Koop line's
  handle isn't in woning_applies_by_product. Rule 6 still strips the property from a Koop line
  whose package (woning_applies_fks) doesn't offer Woning at all. A line with Afname: Kopen on
  any other product is left alone here; Overzicht blocks checkout for it.

  The same rules are exposed as window.zvCartGuard.planFix(cart), which returns the one fix
  or null. Overzicht's checkout button runs it on a fresh /cart.js before it navigates.

  NAMI packages: this guard must NEVER pick one of the three NAMI install options for the
  customer — there isn't one correct answer, only the customer's own choice on Overzicht
  (required radio group, see sections/zv-checkout-overview.liquid). A NAMI cart with none of
  the three is left alone; that's the expected state until the customer chooses.

  A package line that arrives WITHOUT the 50% discount (e.g. the Shopify discount was
  deactivated) is not something this script can fix. Overzicht blocks checkout for it
  server-side instead (`cart_pkg_undiscounted` in zv-checkout-overview.liquid), so a customer
  can never pay 3 full months.

  Silent no-op throughout if a variant id can't be resolved, or if a fetch fails (e.g.
  offline) — Overzicht also fails safe server-side (its checkout gate blocks regardless of
  whether this script runs).

  Params: activation_variant_id (Climax installation, CL003), sub_type,
  nami_geen_variant_id, nami_telefonisch_variant_id, nami_huis_variant_id, pkg_qty
  (zv_promo_package_qty), and the package product handles inzicht_handle, zeker_handle,
  alert_handle (NAMI) and beschermd_handle, protect_handle (Climax); for the Woning rules
  woning_variant_ids (zv-woning-variants' output, 0 for an unresolved product),
  woning_applies_by_product and woning_applies_fks_by_product (zv_woning_applies_by_product /
  zv_woning_applies_fks_by_product, both parallel to it), woning_v1, woning_v2
  (zv_woning_1_value / _2_value), woning_legacy (zv_woning_legacy_prefix), woning_applies
  (zv_woning_applies_handles) and woning_applies_fks (zv_woning_applies_fks); for rule 7
  rider_pairs (zv-addon-riders' output) — passed explicitly because `render` doesn't inherit
  the caller's scope. koop_map (zv_koop_fk_by_handle, 'handle:finder_key|...') names the Koop
  products.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if pkg_qty > 0 -%}
<script>
(function () {
  if (window.__zvCartGuardRan) return;
  window.__zvCartGuardRan = true;
  var ACTIVATION_ID = {{ activation_variant_id | json }};
  var SUB_TYPE = {{ sub_type | json }};
  var PKG_QTY = {{ pkg_qty | json }};
  var NAMI_IDS = [{{ nami_geen_variant_id | json }}, {{ nami_telefonisch_variant_id | json }}, {{ nami_huis_variant_id | json }}]
    .filter(function (id) { return id != null; })
    .map(String);
  var NAMI_PKG_HANDLES = [{{ inzicht_handle | json }}, {{ zeker_handle | json }}, {{ alert_handle | json }}].filter(Boolean);
  var CLIMAX_PKG_HANDLES = [{{ beschermd_handle | json }}, {{ protect_handle | json }}].filter(Boolean);
  var WONING_V1 = {{ woning_v1 | json }}, WONING_V2 = {{ woning_v2 | json }}, WONING_LEGACY = {{ woning_legacy | json }};
  var WONING_APPLIES = String({{ woning_applies | json }} || '').split('|').filter(Boolean);
  var WONING_APPLIES_FKS = String({{ woning_applies_fks | json }} || '').split('|').filter(Boolean);
  // One entry per Woning product (NAMI, Climax): its variant id, the Huren package handles
  // whose floors it carries (applies), and the same packages' finder_keys (appliesFks) — a
  // Koop line is a different handle (koop_map) so rule 5 matches it by finder_key instead.
  // An unresolved product (0) is left out: property only.
  var WONING_PRODUCTS = (function () {
    var ids = String({{ woning_variant_ids | json }} || '').split('|');
    var applies = String({{ woning_applies_by_product | json }} || '').split('|');
    var appliesFks = String({{ woning_applies_fks_by_product | json }} || '').split('|');
    return ids.map(function (id, i) {
      return {
        id: id,
        applies: String(applies[i] || '').split(',').filter(Boolean),
        appliesFks: String(appliesFks[i] || '').split(',').filter(Boolean)
      };
    }).filter(function (wp) { return wp.id && wp.id !== '0'; });
  })();
  // Rider pairs (rule 7): lead variant -> rider variant.
  var RIDERS = String({{ rider_pairs | json }} || '').split('|').map(function (s) { return s.split(':'); })
    .filter(function (p) { return p[0] && p[1]; }).map(function (p) { return { lead: p[0], rider: p[1] }; });
  // Koop product handle -> finder_key; a Koop package line also carries Afname: Kopen.
  var KOOP_FK = {};
  String({{ koop_map | json }} || '').split('|').forEach(function (pair) {
    var kv = pair.split(':');
    if (kv[0] && kv[1]) KOOP_FK[kv[0]] = kv[1];
  });
  var NAMI_FKS = ['aware', 'aware_plus', 'secure'];
  function isKoopProp(it) { return (it.properties || {})['Afname'] === 'Kopen'; }
  function isKoop(it) { return isKoopProp(it) && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(KOOP_FK, it.handle); }
  function isKoopClimax(it) { return isKoop(it) && NAMI_FKS.indexOf(KOOP_FK[it.handle]) === -1; }

  // A Woning property value -> floors, the same mapping as snippets/zv-woning-floors.liquid.
  function woningFloors(value) {
    var v = value == null ? '' : String(value);
    if (!v) return 0;
    if (WONING_V2 && v === WONING_V2) return 2;
    if (WONING_V1 && v === WONING_V1) return 1;
    return (WONING_LEGACY && v.indexOf(WONING_LEGACY) === 0) ? 1 : 0;
  }
  function hasWoningProp(it) {
    var p = it.properties || {};
    return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(p, 'Woning') && p['Woning'] != null && p['Woning'] !== '';
  }

  function post(url, body) {
    return window.fetch(url, {
      method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify(body)
    }).then(function (r) { if (r.ok) window.location.reload(); });
  }

  // The rules below, as a pure function of a /cart.js response: returns the ONE fix to
  // apply as { url, body }, or null when the cart is in shape. Exposed as
  // window.zvCartGuard.planFix so Overzicht's checkout button can re-check a fresh cart
  // on click with these same rules instead of a copy of them.
  function planFix(cart) {
    var items = (cart && cart.items) || [];
    var isWoningLine = function (it) {
      return WONING_PRODUCTS.some(function (wp) { return String(it.variant_id) === wp.id; });
    };
    var isPkg = function (it) {
      return !isWoningLine(it) && !isKoopProp(it) && it.product_type === SUB_TYPE && (NAMI_PKG_HANDLES.indexOf(it.handle) !== -1 || CLIMAX_PKG_HANDLES.indexOf(it.handle) !== -1);
    };
    var isActivation = function (it) { return ACTIVATION_ID != null && String(it.variant_id) === String(ACTIVATION_ID); };
    var namiLines = items.filter(function (it) { return NAMI_IDS.indexOf(String(it.variant_id)) !== -1; });
    var pkgLines = items.filter(isPkg);
    var koopLines = items.filter(isKoop);
    var hasClimaxPkg = pkgLines.some(function (it) { return CLIMAX_PKG_HANDLES.indexOf(it.handle) !== -1; }) || koopLines.some(isKoopClimax);
    var activationLines = items.filter(isActivation);

    // 1. Duplicate NAMI install lines: keep the most recently added.
    if (namiLines.length > 1) {
      var keepId = String(namiLines[namiLines.length - 1].variant_id);
      var namiUpdates = {};
      namiLines.forEach(function (it) {
        var vid = String(it.variant_id);
        if (vid !== keepId) namiUpdates[vid] = 0;
      });
      return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: namiUpdates } };
    }

    // 2. Quantities, keyed by line key so each line is set on its own.
    var qtyUpdates = {};
    var seenPkgVariants = {};
    pkgLines.forEach(function (it) {
      var vid = String(it.variant_id);
      if (seenPkgVariants[vid]) { qtyUpdates[it.key] = 0; return; }
      seenPkgVariants[vid] = true;
      if (it.quantity !== PKG_QTY) qtyUpdates[it.key] = PKG_QTY;
    });
    // A Koop line is a one-time purchase: quantity 1, one line per Koop product.
    var seenKoopVariants = {};
    koopLines.forEach(function (it) {
      var vid = String(it.variant_id);
      if (seenKoopVariants[vid]) { qtyUpdates[it.key] = 0; return; }
      seenKoopVariants[vid] = true;
      if (it.quantity !== 1) qtyUpdates[it.key] = 1;
    });
    namiLines.concat(activationLines).forEach(function (it) {
      if (it.quantity !== 1 && qtyUpdates[it.key] == null) qtyUpdates[it.key] = 1;
    });
    if (Object.keys(qtyUpdates).length) return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: qtyUpdates } };

    // 3. A Climax package needs the one fixed Climax installation line.
    //    update.js with an absolute quantity of 1 (it adds the variant when it's missing),
    //    never add.js: add.js increments, so two overlapping guard runs (a fast /cart ->
    //    Overzicht click, or two tabs) would each add 1 and stack CL003 to quantity 2.
    if (hasClimaxPkg && ACTIVATION_ID != null && !activationLines.length) {
      var setActivation = {};
      setActivation[ACTIVATION_ID] = 1;
      return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: setActivation } };
    }

    // 4. The Climax installation line never stays in a cart without a Climax package.
    if (!hasClimaxPkg && activationLines.length) {
      var rm = {};
      activationLines.forEach(function (it) { rm[it.key] = 0; });
      return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: rm } };
    }

    // 5. The Woning lines: per Woning product, one line at pkg_qty x its own package lines' floors.
    for (var w = 0; w < WONING_PRODUCTS.length; w++) {
      var wp = WONING_PRODUCTS[w];
      var floors = 0;
      pkgLines.forEach(function (it) {
        if (wp.applies.indexOf(it.handle) !== -1) floors += woningFloors((it.properties || {})['Woning']);
      });
      koopLines.forEach(function (it) {
        if (wp.appliesFks.indexOf(KOOP_FK[it.handle]) !== -1) floors += woningFloors((it.properties || {})['Woning']);
      });
      var target = PKG_QTY * floors;
      var woningLines = items.filter(function (it) { return String(it.variant_id) === wp.id; });
      if (woningLines.length > 1) {
        var merge = {};
        woningLines.forEach(function (it, i) { merge[it.key] = i === 0 ? target : 0; });
        return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: merge } };
      }
      if (woningLines.length === 1 && woningLines[0].quantity !== target) {
        var setWoning = {};
        setWoning[woningLines[0].key] = target;   // 0 removes it
        return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: setWoning } };
      }
      // Missing: update.js with an absolute quantity by variant id adds it, and two overlapping
      // guard runs can't stack it (same reason as rule 3).
      if (!woningLines.length && target > 0) {
        var addWoning = {};
        addWoning[wp.id] = target;
        return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: addWoning } };
      }
    }

    // 6. A package that doesn't offer Woning never carries it: delete the property, keep the quantity.
    var strayWoning = pkgLines.filter(function (it) { return WONING_APPLIES.indexOf(it.handle) === -1 && hasWoningProp(it); })
      .concat(koopLines.filter(function (it) { return WONING_APPLIES_FKS.indexOf(KOOP_FK[it.handle]) === -1 && hasWoningProp(it); }))[0];
    if (strayWoning) {
      var keep = {}, cp = strayWoning.properties || {};
      for (var pk in cp) { if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(cp, pk) && pk !== 'Woning') keep[pk] = cp[pk]; }
      return { url: '/cart/change.js', body: { id: strayWoning.key, quantity: strayWoning.quantity, properties: keep } };
    }

    // 7. Riders: one rider line at quantity PKG_QTY while a lead line is in the cart, none otherwise.
    for (var r = 0; r < RIDERS.length; r++) {
      var rd = RIDERS[r];
      var hasLead = items.some(function (it) { return String(it.variant_id) === rd.lead; });
      var riderLines = items.filter(function (it) { return String(it.variant_id) === rd.rider; });
      var riderTarget = hasLead ? PKG_QTY : 0;
      if (riderLines.length > 1 || (riderLines.length === 1 && riderLines[0].quantity !== riderTarget)) {
        var setRider = {};
        riderLines.forEach(function (it, i) { setRider[it.key] = i === 0 ? riderTarget : 0; });
        return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: setRider } };
      }
      if (!riderLines.length && riderTarget > 0) {
        var addRider = {};
        addRider[rd.rider] = riderTarget;   // absolute, by variant id: two guard runs can't stack it (rule 3)
        return { url: '/cart/update.js', body: { updates: addRider } };
      }
    }
    return null;
  }

  window.zvCartGuard = { planFix: planFix };

  window.fetch('/cart.js').then(function (r) { return r.json(); }).then(function (cart) {
    var fix = planFix(cart);
    if (fix) return post(fix.url, fix.body);
  }).catch(function () { /* fail safe: server-side gate (Overzicht) still blocks checkout */ });
})();
</script>
{%- endif -%}
